An old Bloomwarden leans on a staff grown, not carved, watching the bog the way a teacher watches a slow class.
"You'll have heard the marsh keeps a ledger. True. What they leave out is who's reading it back."
"Every creature down here was a god's leftover, climber. Tend the leftovers gently and you tend the god. That's the whole craft."
"The Iron Guild builds better gods. The Pale Court buries the old ones for parts. We Bloomwardens just keep them alive long enough to forgive us."
[He taps the staff once. Something underfoot, ancient and patient, taps back.]
"Learn the gentle way first. The marsh forgives a slow hand. It has never once forgiven a quick one."
